  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) is the best result so far at 0.591 acc, showing that multiprofile+avgpool is a strong setting and that RNA dominates image (0.591 vs 0.208). The only RNA encoder tested is pca_n2000, leaving significant uncertainty about whether a learned encoder (scvi_n200) captures biological structure better than linear PCA. This experiment (config_005) changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding multiprofile+avgpool fixed, directly isolating the encoder effect against the known baseline of 0.591. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information single-variable test: if scvi_n200 improves, it justifies investing in learned encoders for multimodal configs; if it does not, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and we can redirect budget toward fusion/image questions with confidence."
}

